  "reason": "Evidence: config_043 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.6287 acc. In singleprofile, concat and weighted fusion are nearly identical (0.5266 vs 0.5232), and in multiprofile with resnet50 we've only tested concat (config_008: 0.6186). We have no multiprofile+ViT data point for weighted fusion. Question: Does weighted fusion match or beat concat in the best-performing multiprofile+ViT+avgpool setup? This isolates the single variable of fusion strategy while holding all other choices at their empirically best values. Rationale: Under a limited budget, a one-variable extension of the top configuration is the most efficient way to either confirm concat's advantage (locking in the design) or discover that weighted fusion is equally good (freeing a design degree for future experiments). It avoids the risk of changing multiple variables (e.g., aggregation + fusion) and directly informs whether the current best can be improved or whether we should pivot to exploring other axes (RNA encoder, aggregation) next."
